From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Erik Bourget <erik@ebourget.net>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 22:48:16 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] ASoC: tas2764: Free the fault IRQ when the component is
 removed

The component probe requests the fault IRQ as a devres of the I2C
device, which stays bound when the sound card is torn down.  Every
rebind of the card probes the component again and adds another handler
for the same amp on the line: after two rebinds the J713's four amps
had twelve handlers on their shared IRQ, each fault interrupt ran every
one of them, and each does six I2C reads.

Request the IRQ without devres and free it in the component remove.  A
devres would not do: when the I2C device itself is unbound, its devres
release frees the IRQ first and only then unregisters the component, so
a devm_free_irq() in the remove would find nothing and warn.  Request it
as the probe's last step, so that a probe that fails later does not
leave a handler behind either.

Signed-off-by: Erik Bourget <erik@ebourget.net>
[eryk: request the IRQ without devres: on an I2C unbind the devres
 release frees it before the component is removed, and the devm_free_irq()
 in the remove then warns]
Signed-off-by: Eryk Wieliczko <eryk@wieliczko.ninja>
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
(cherry picked from commit 5aa11dee57d3c4ed1a55493ae8a1d81d83b16248)
Signed-off-by: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
---
 sound/soc/codecs/tas2764.c | 32 ++++++++++++++++++++++++--------
 1 file changed, 24 insertions(+), 8 deletions(-)

diff --git a/sound/soc/codecs/tas2764.c b/sound/soc/codecs/tas2764.c
index 0775206da7..025a111e26 100644
--- a/sound/soc/codecs/tas2764.c
+++ b/sound/soc/codecs/tas2764.c
@@ -60,6 +60,8 @@ struct tas2764_priv {
 	struct regmap *regmap;
 	struct device *dev;
 	int irq;
+	/* Set while the component holds the fault IRQ */
+	bool irq_requested;
 	enum tas2764_devid devid;
 
 	int v_sense_slot;
@@ -1061,14 +1063,6 @@ static int tas2764_codec_probe(struct snd_soc_component *component)
 		ret = snd_soc_component_write(tas2764->component, TAS2764_INT_MASK4, 0xff);
 		if (ret < 0)
 			return ret;
-
-		ret = devm_request_threaded_irq(tas2764->dev, tas2764->irq, NULL, tas2764_irq,
-						IRQF_ONESHOT | IRQF_SHARED | IRQF_TRIGGER_LOW,
-						"tas2764", tas2764);
-		if (ret && tas2764->sdz_group)
-			return dev_err_probe(tas2764->dev, ret, "SDZ group needs its fault IRQ\n");
-		if (ret)
-			dev_warn(tas2764->dev, "failed to request IRQ: %d\n", ret);
 	}
 
 	if (tas2764->i_sense_slot != -1 && tas2764->v_sense_slot != -1) {
@@ -1107,6 +1101,23 @@ static int tas2764_codec_probe(struct snd_soc_component *component)
 		break;
 	}
 
+	/*
+	 * Last, so that no failure leaves the handler behind. The component owns the IRQ and
+	 * the remove frees it; not a devres of the I2C device, which outlives the component
+	 * and, on an unbind, would release the IRQ before the component is removed.
+	 */
+	if (tas2764->irq) {
+		ret = request_threaded_irq(tas2764->irq, NULL, tas2764_irq,
+					   IRQF_ONESHOT | IRQF_SHARED | IRQF_TRIGGER_LOW,
+					   "tas2764", tas2764);
+		if (ret && tas2764->sdz_group)
+			return dev_err_probe(tas2764->dev, ret, "SDZ group needs its fault IRQ\n");
+		if (ret)
+			dev_warn(tas2764->dev, "failed to request IRQ: %d\n", ret);
+		else
+			tas2764->irq_requested = true;
+	}
+
 	return 0;
 }
 
@@ -1114,6 +1125,11 @@ static void tas2764_codec_remove(struct snd_soc_component *component)
 {
 	struct tas2764_priv *tas2764 = snd_soc_component_get_drvdata(component);
 
+	if (tas2764->irq_requested) {
+		free_irq(tas2764->irq, tas2764);
+		tas2764->irq_requested = false;
+	}
+
 	tas2764_flush_shutdown(tas2764);
 
 	/* A failed group's supply was forced off: there is no enable left to balance. */
